{
  "notes": [
    "Alternative tile art, for comparing new art against the placeholder tiles without replacing them. The map editor's 'New tile art' switch stores the chosen set (or 'none' for the original art) in the browser (localStorage) and it applies to every map view after a reload.",
    "defaultSet: the set used when the browser has no stored choice.",
    "folder: where the set's PNGs live; files: the tile images it replaces (same file names as public/art/tiles/). Tiles not listed keep their current art.",
    "effects: also draw soft contact shadows on floors next to blocks and coloured light pools round glowing tiles. glows: tile id -> light colour; activeGlows: tile id -> light colour while the tile is active (a live hazard).",
    "animations: tile id -> light-only overlay images (in the set's folder) drawn over the tile and animated: pulse (slow breathing glow), blink (status lights switching on and off), flicker (an unsteady screen). Each tile on a map is offset in time so machines don't flash together.",
    "wallVariants: wall id -> { share, variants }. In the tall-wall views (exploration, Combat Type 1, the map editor) about share of that wall's tiles are drawn as one of the variants instead (Star Trek wall fittings: LCARS display, EPS conduit, Jefferies tube hatch, computer bank), chosen from the tile's position so a map always looks the same. Never on a panel half with a window. Presentation only.",
    "v2 covers every tile, drawn at 4x resolution (256 x 384; the views scale every tile image to the 64 x 96 slot): the Starship & Station tiles by scripts/makeTilesV2.mjs, all the others by scripts/makeTilesV2World.mjs. The long wall fittings (lcarsPanel etc.) already use v2 bulkhead art. Presentation only."
  ],
  "defaultSet": "v2",
